mod_audio_fork: refuse runtime unload.

"unload mod_audio_fork" (and "reload mod_audio_fork", or a graceful "fsctl shutdown") runs
mod_audio_fork_shutdown -> fork_cleanup -> AudioPipe::deinitialize(), which calls
lws_context_destroy() on every libwebsockets context from the FreeSWITCH thread while the detached
service threads are still inside lws_service() on those contexts; FreeSWITCH then dlcloses the module
under the running threads. Reproduced on FreeSWITCH 1.10.12: "malloc(): unsorted double linked list
corrupted", abort, every call dropped.

The load function now returns SWITCH_STATUS_NOUNLOAD, which FreeSWITCH treats as a successful load
(a critical load still succeeds) and records as a permanent module: "unload"/"reload" answer
"Module is not unloadable" and process shutdown skips the module's teardown. Loading, the API and
every call path are unchanged. Upgrading the module still means restarting FreeSWITCH, which the
container image requires anyway.

Against drachtio-freeswitch-modules 88e1465908a89bed5c95d336aa53a3899bb5abb5, modules/mod_audio_fork,
after 0001. Apply from the module directory: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 --batch
--- a/mod_audio_fork.c
+++ b/mod_audio_fork.c
@@ -330,7 +330,11 @@
 
 	/* indicate that the module should continue to be loaded */
   //mod_running = 1;
-	return SWITCH_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+	/* Loaded for the life of the process: AudioPipe::deinitialize() destroys the libwebsockets
+	   contexts while the detached service threads still run lws_service() on them, which corrupts
+	   the heap and aborts FreeSWITCH. NOUNLOAD makes "unload"/"reload" refuse and skips that
+	   teardown at shutdown. */
+	return SWITCH_STATUS_NOUNLOAD;
 }
 
